        "subject": "LU-20581 tests: size the router buffers in test_50",
        "message": "LU-20581 tests: size the router buffers in test_50\n\ntest_50 enabled routing without setting the router buffer\nparameters, so LNet allocated the default pool: LNET_NRB_LARGE\n1 MiB buffers, about 1 GiB. lnet_nrb_*_calculate() divides by\nLNET_CPT_NUMBER and then allocates per CPT, so the total is the\nsame whatever the CPU count, and a small node cannot spare it.\nThe import failed with -ENOMEM.\n\nSet small and large to the counts setup_router_test() uses, and\ntiny to a flat 16, which is enough because test_50 never routes\ntraffic. They are read-only parameters, so the test now loads\nlnet itself instead of reusing an already configured one.\nconfigure_dlc() takes module options to that end.\n\nFixes: 83fa59b2d5a6 (\"LU-19200 tests: Check routing/buffers/numa import\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I254f899634bbcedb62d4e87d347d2f83f34c245e\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67929\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Cyril Bordage <cbordage@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
